  "tail": "Batch 54 draft authoring is complete. The A page contains the FDR/FWER definitions, BH procedure, leave-one-out lemma, and theorem; the B page contains the two-test example.\n\n- **Ready:** the two definitions and the leave-one-out lemma.\n- **Escalated:** the theorem and example. The plan requires batch 52’s `valid-p-values-bonferroni-and-simultaneous-coverage` page, but its manifest had no item IDs or supplier bodies at initial inspection. The exact page and affected claims are recorded for reconciliation.\n- The theorem uses a direct leave-one-out identity instead of reproducing BH95’s induction proof. Its hypotheses and claim are preserved; the route variation is documented for owner review.\n- BH95 and the [Stanford lecture notes](https://web.stanford.edu/class/archive/stats/stats200/stats200.1172/Lecture11.pdf) passed full-text fetch checks. The [BY01 Project Euclid URL](https://projecteuclid.org/download/pdf_1/euclid.aos/1013699998) returned only a short HTML wrapper after six attempts; its drop and complete local proof alternatives are recorded.\n\n**Checks:** scoped dependency levels (0, 0, 1, 2, 3), manifest dependencies, content policy, focused depcheck, proof contracts, precheck, proof layout, rendercheck, and source-fetch resolution passed. Proof layout checked 5 items and 13 steps with no defects. Run-wide proof-contract coverage remains blocked by the empty `stratified-sampling-and-allocation` manifest in another batch.\n\nA `depcheck --help` invocation unexpectedly ran the whole-corpus check and failed on unrelated published-item audit entries; it made no changes. The subsequent focused batch check passed.\n\n**Batch evidence:** [A/B manifest](research/statistical-models-experiments-62-batch-54.pages.json), [proof contracts](research/statistical-models-experiments-62-batch-54.proof-contracts.json), [source coverage](research/statistical-models-experiments-62-batch-54.coverage.json), [cross-batch dependencies](research/statistical-models-experiments-62-batch-54.cross-batch-dependencies.json), and [notes](research/statistical-models-experiments-62-batch-54.notes.md)."
